[ti:Day 20]

[00:00.00]rampant [ˈræmpənt]a. 猖獗的；蔓延的 例 Rampant inflation means that our savings will shrink a lot.
[00:09.24]caption [ˈkæpʃn]n. 标题；字幕；说明 vt. 加上标题，加 上说明 例 Please suggest a caption in the comments thread below. 搭 caption scanner 字幕扫描器 / under the caption of 在…的标题下
[00:24.60]flair [fleə(r)]n. 鉴别力；天赋，资质；眼光 例 The single biggest factor in the success of any business, is its human capital, including the flair, talent and productivity of its workers. 搭 have a flair for 具备…的天赋
[00:44.64]sample [ˈsɑːmpl]n. 样品，样本；试样；范例 a. 样品 的；试样的
[00:49.08]raffle [ˈræfl]n. 抽奖售货；杂物 vt. 以抽奖法出售 vi. 抽 奖 adhere to 黏着，附着；遵循 例 To make sure your commodity investing is successful, you must adhere to the SMART strategy, that is, your goals must be speciflc, measurable, accountable, realistic and timecentric.
[01:14.04]variation [ˌveəriˈeɪʃn]n. 变化；变动；变更；波动 例 There has been no variation in the price of vegetables for two months. Laytime means time allowed to load or unload the cargo on the vessel.
[01:32.16]compile [kəmˈpaɪl]vt. 汇编，编制；编纂；编译；收集(资 料等) 例 You can compile code and run it in its default scope.
[01:42.12]unleash [ʌnˈliːʃ]vt. 解除…的束缚；放开；发动 例 You might find a new way to unleash more consumer demand by boosting green consumption.
[01:54.72]disequilibrium [ˌdɪsˌiːkwɪˈlɪbriəm]n. 失去平衡，不平衡
[02:00.00]characteristic [ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk]n. 典型；特征，特点 a. 典型 的；有特点的 例 Autonomy is the characteristic of all successful institutions.
[02:12.84]signatory [ˈsɪɡnətri]n. 签名人；签约国；(协议等的)签署者 a. 签署的；签约的
[02:18.60]agreed [əˈɡriːd]a. 商定的，同意的
[02:21.48]frugal [ˈfruːɡl]a. 节俭的，朴素的；花钱少的 例 We should advocate a more frugal lifestyle so as to reduce the growing scale of waste pollution. 搭 be frugal of 节省
[02:36.24]crude [kruːd]a. 天然的，未加工的；概约的 例 Our store can supply the crude Coconut flbre from Thailand, the Philippines and Vietnam.
[02:48.48]rendering [ˈrendərɪŋ]n. 提供；给予；翻译；示意图
[02:52.56]bumpily [ˈbʌmpili]ad. 崎岖地；颠簸地 例 The car bounced along the mountain road bumpily.
[03:00.84]brick-and-mortar [ˌbrɪkəndˈmɔːtə(r)]a. 砖瓦加水泥的(常用来比喻 传统企业)；(有)实体的 例 In the brick-and-mortar travel agent model, a trained agent meets with the traveller in person or establishes a relationship over the phone.
[03:22.56]feeble [ˈfiːbl]a. 无力的；软弱的；无效的；不充分的， 不成熟的 例 Tighter credit conditions are sapping already feeble demand.
[03:33.48]implication [ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn]n. 暗示；牵连，卷入；影响 例 The phenomenon has an interest ing implication for our company's future.
[03:45.60]equality [iˈkwɒləti]n. 相等；平等 例 We're born of equality though develop to be different. 搭 be on an equality with 与…平等 / racial equality 种族平等
[03:59.40]wrap-up [ˌræpˈʌp]n. 综合报道，简讯；新闻提要；不费事 的快速推销
[04:04.08]escort [ˈeskɔːt]n. 护卫，护送；押运；护航 [ɪˈskɔːt]vt. 护卫，护送；为…护航 例 Merchant ships are escorted by warships since this is the area where pirates harried. 搭 under the escort of 在…的护送下
[04:21.60]bankruptcy [ˈbæŋkrʌptsi]n. 破产，倒闭；彻底失败 例 A great many small businesses went into bankruptcy during the financial crisis in 2008.
[04:34.80]gauge [ɡeɪdʒ]n. 标准尺寸，标准规格；测量仪器；(估 计、判断的)手段 vt. (精确)测量；估量 例 The amount of money one makes is not the only gauge of one's success. 搭 take the gauge 估计；判断 / temperature gauge 温度计
[04:52.32]literate [ˈlɪtərət]a. 有读写能力的；受过教育的 例 One of the disadvantages of the Internet is that you have to be literate to use it.
[05:04.32]flanker [ˈflæŋkə(r)]n. 名牌辅助产品；系列新产品 例 Microsoft has focused more on its flankers such as the Xbox 360 to bring the Media Centre experience to the big-screen TV.
[05:20.52]hyperinflation [ˌhaɪpərɪnˈfleɪʃn]n. 极度通货膨胀；恶性通货膨胀 例 Hyperinflation invariably emerges in a deflationary environment of weak economic activities.
[05:36.12]multi-brand [ˈmʌltibrænd]a. 多品牌的
[05:39.72]elasticity [ˌiːlæˈstɪsəti]n. (需求等的)弹性，伸缩性；灵活性 例 The analysis for the market demand elasticity is very important in enterprise operations.
[05:54.24]satisfaction [ˌsætɪsˈfækʃn]n. 满意，满足；满意度；赔偿， 清偿；赔偿物 搭 in satisfaction of 作为…的赔偿 / make satisfaction for 赔偿…，偿还…
[06:05.88]expedite [ˈekspədaɪt]vt. 加快，促进；发送，急送 a. 迅速 的；便利的
