[06:22.68]swap [swɒp]v. 交换；用…做交易 n. 交换；交易
[06:25.92]uncertainty [ʌnˈsɜːtnti]n. 不确定；不稳定；不可靠 例 Business is full of uncertainty. Insurance companies do not cover any accident which is caused by an act of God.
[06:41.52]disparity [dɪˈspærəti]n. 不等；不一致，不相称；悬殊 例 There is a growing disparity between the rich and the poor.
[06:51.84]indulgence [ɪnˈdʌldʒəns]n. 沉溺；放纵；纵容，迁就；嗜好 例 Self-forgiveness is just another form of self indulgence.
[07:02.64]disgruntled [dɪsˈɡrʌntld]a. 〈口〉不满的；不高兴的 例 He is disgruntled at the working conditions.
[07:11.76]negative [ˈneɡətɪv]a. 消极的；负面的；否定的；[数]负 的；相反的，反面的
