[07:26.64]trade-off [ˈtreɪdɒf]n. 物物交换；权衡；平衡 例 There should be a trade-off between doing the job accurately and doing it quickly.
[07:38.76]gratitude [ˈɡrætɪtjuːd]n. 感激；感谢 例 I wish to express my gratitude to Kathy for her immense practical help with the work. 搭 express gratitude to sb. 向某人表示感谢 / out of gratitude 出于感激
[07:56.52]associate [əˈsəʊʃieɪt]vt. 使发生联系；使结合在一起；宣布 赞同 vi. 交往；结交 [əˈsəʊʃiət]n. 合伙人 a. 副的；非正式的 搭 associate with sb. 与某人交往
[08:08.04]niche [niːʃ]n. 合适的职业；(亦称作niche market) 有利 可图的市场(或形势等) 例 Finding a niche market in business is the key to success.
[08:19.56]enrichment [ɪnˈrɪtʃmənt]n. 富裕；富足 例 Life enrichment might be a result of working experience abroad.
